==Galician==

===Etymology===
From Old Galician and {{inh|gl|roa-opt|aprender}} (13<sup>th</sup> century, {{w|Cantigas de Santa Maria}}), from {{inh|gl|la|apprendere}}, alternative form of {{m|la|apprehendere}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|apprehendō}}. Compare the borrowed doublet {{doublet|gl|apreender|notext=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|[apɾenˈdeɾ]}}

===Verb===
{{gl-verb|aprend|er}}

# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[learn]]
#: {{syn|gl|deprender}}
# {{lb|gl|transitive}} to [[teach]]
#: {{uxi|gl|O meu tío '''aprendeume''' a nadar.|My uncle '''taught me''' to swim.}}
#: {{syn|gl|ensinar}}

